the ps5 comes with an 825 gigabyte ssd  for storage  around 667 gigabytes of which is free  for you to use  which seems like a lot of free space  until you realize that games like call  of duty black ops cold war  can hit well over a hundred gigabytes if  you have the base game  warzone and all the multiplayer modes  installed oh  and you need to have ps5 games installed  on the internal drive  at the moment you can't expand your  internal storage but sony has stated  that ps5 owners will be able to  at some point in the future until then  here are some top tips to stop  you from running out of space one of the  crucial things you'll need to do with  your next gen console is keep an  eye on your available storage space it's  never fun purchasing a new game and then  discovering that you lack the open  storage to download it  every game you have in your library will  take up space in your console's ssd  and this also includes game disks that  will need to load data onto your drive  while you may have the urge to download  all your most wanted games at once  it's best to focus on the essentials you  will always have access to purchased  games in your account library so even  when you delete the game from your drive  you can still download it again  later if you want to revisit the game a  really solid tip though  is to turn off auto updates go into your  system settings and disable the auto  update feature  generally updates for your current set  of installed games will be downloaded  automatically  to your drive when your console is  online these include games you may have  finished or may not get back to anytime  soon  to optimize space be sure to switch this  off and focus on downloading updates for  games you want to play regularly  one interesting change that came with  the playstation's trophy system is that  the ps5 will now save a clip  of the exact moment you earn a trophy by  default the ps5 will automatically save  around a 15 second long video of  every trophy you unlock in a game this  innovation can be great for those who  want to save a particular moment  however these video files will add up  over time  resulting in a bulky media folder filled  with videos  of you earning all sorts of trophies  even the bronze ones  that didn't actually require that much  effort to save on space  we highly recommend disabling this  feature outright  if you do want to save a moment when you  earn a trophy then the ps5's create  button will allow you to save  video files capturing several minutes  from your recent gameplay session  so once something exciting happens just  tap the create button and the moment  will be saved  as a video it's always good to keep an  eye out for the growing size of your  media folder so every once in a while  it'll be a good idea to start clearing  out old videos that are taking up too  much space  the ps5 sophisticated ssd is an  impressive storage device and it also  shows off the speed  in next-gen loading times you may be  tempted to load everything onto the ssd  but like i mentioned earlier  you can't put ps5 games on there so a  better option is to use your external  storage device  solely for backwards compatible games  plugged in through a usb you can  download your ps4 games  straight onto that external device and  play them from there  your load times may be a little bit  slower because you're using an external  device but  think of all the space you'll be saving  the ps5 lineup includes a set of games  that are available for the playstation 4  as well  along with letting ps4 users experience  some of the latest games  these cross-gen titles also allow  players to carry their progress to the  ps5  however a surprising quirk that comes  from this is that it's possible to  download ps4  and ps5 versions of the same game  simultaneously  on your next gen console to avoid this  from happening to you  download the games you purchased  straight from your library instead  in order to make sure you have the  proper game downloaded and set  highlight the game on the cross media  bar and hit the options button on your  controller  to bring up a sub menu select the game  version option to see the list of  available versions for the game you have  installed and select the ps5 edition  even after installing the ps5 version  the media bar can sometimes default to  the ps4 version  prompting you to download that before  proceeding with the game so make sure  you have the ps5 version set and let's  hope that sony fixes this issue  soon we've got so much more about the  playstation 5 including graphics  comparisons  loading comparisons and even hidden  features on the console that you may not  know about  so make sure to check out gamespot.com  and youtube.com  [Music]  gamespot  you
 

